     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From eleven to one hundred",
     "texto": [
      "From once to quince, each number is a new word: **once, doce, trece, catorce, quince**.\n\nFrom dieciséis to diecinueve everything is written together: **dieciséis, diecisiete, dieciocho, diecinueve**.\n\nVeinte also has its own family: **veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés…**\n\nFrom treinta y uno on, it is separated with **y**: **treinta y uno**, **cuarenta y dos**, **cincuenta y tres**.\n\nAnd the end: **cien**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "One word or two",
     "texto": [
      "Notice the difference:\n\n- **dieciséis, veintiuno, veintidós**: a single word\n- **treinta y uno, cuarenta y dos**: three words, with **y** in the middle\n\nThe change happens at **treinta**: up to veintinueve everything goes together, and from there on it separates."
